25","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.000242854,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.0525761,"nucleus_score":-3.81772,"pct_ad":0.116728,"pct_control":0.127262,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.950695,"donor_log2fc":0.0747005,"donor_lfcse":0.18129,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.0024884}],"modules":[],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000243725","entrez_id":["7268"],"uniprot":["O95801"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a protein that contains tetratricopeptide (TPR) repeats, which often mediate protein-protein interactions and chaperone activity. The encoded protein interacts with heat shock proteins 70 and 90. Alternative splicing results in multiple transcript variants. Naturally-occuring readthrough transcription occurs from upstream gene MROH (maestro heat-like repeat family member 7) to this gene. [provided by RefSeq, Apr 2014].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"O95801","text":"Co-chaperone that recruits molecular chaperones Hsp90 (HSC82 and HSP82) and Hsp70 (SSA1) to nascent polypeptides, facilitating their proper folding into functional proteins (PubMed:18320024). Client proteins include eukaryotic elongation factor eEF2, a key player in cellular translation. Stimulates SSA1 ATPase activity, but not Hsp90 ATPase activity (By similarity). Promotes Sendai virus (SeV)-induced host cell innate immune responses (PubMed:29251827)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}